  <!-- START HERE: CANONICAL PATH FROM DISCOVERY TO FIRST PROJECT (Issue #8) -->
  <section class="start-section" id="start">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-head w-full text-center flex flex-col items-center justify-center">
        <div class="sub-badge" data-i18n="start.badge">Start Here</div>
        <h2 data-i18n="start.title">From Discovery to Your First Krewire Project</h2>
        <p data-i18n="start.subtitle">This portal is the community front door. It does not host technical documentation: installation, the quickstart, and reference guides live on krewire.com and are maintained alongside the core repository. Follow these four steps in order.</p>
      </div>

      <ol class="start-steps">
        <li class="qs-card">
          <div class="qs-num">1</div>
          <h3 data-i18n="start.s1_title">Understand Krewire</h3>
          <p data-i18n="start.s1_desc">Read the overview to learn what Krewire is, its design principles, and which workload kinds it supports.</p>
          <a href="https://krewire.com/docs" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="start-link" data-i18n="start.s1_link">Read the overview on krewire.com ↗</a>
        </li>
        <li class="qs-card">
          <div class="qs-num">2</div>
          <h3 data-i18n="start.s2_title">Install the kiw CLI</h3>
          <p data-i18n="start.s2_desc">Follow the canonical installation guide. It covers the shell installer, go install, and how to verify the install.</p>
          <a href="https://krewire.com/docs/getting-started/installation" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="start-link" data-i18n="start.s2_link">Installation guide ↗</a>
        </li>
        <li class="qs-card">
          <div class="qs-num">3</div>
          <h3 data-i18n="start.s3_title">Build Your First Project</h3>
          <p data-i18n="start.s3_desc">Work through the hands-on quickstart: scaffold a project, run the dev server, make a change, and build it.</p>
          <a href="https://krewire.com/docs/getting-started#4-hands-on-5-minute-quickstart" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="start-link" data-i18n="start.s3_link">5-minute quickstart ↗</a>
        </li>
        <li class="qs-card">
          <div class="qs-num">4</div>
          <h3 data-i18n="start.s4_title">Choose Your Next Step</h3>
          <p data-i18n="start.s4_desc">Once your first project builds, pick the workload guide that matches what you want to ship next. Ask questions or share what you built in GitHub Discussions.</p>
          <a href="https://krewire.com/docs/workloads" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="start-link" data-i18n="start.s4_link">Workload guides ↗</a>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <h3 class="start-dest-title" data-i18n="start.dest_title">Where Things Live</h3>
      <div class="start-dest-grid">
        <div class="start-dest">
          <span class="start-dest-label" data-i18n="start.d1_label">Discovery &amp; Community</span>
          <p data-i18n="start.d1_desc">This portal: how to get started, how to contribute, and how to support the project.</p>
          <a href="#start" class="start-link" data-i18n="start.d1_link">You are here</a>
        </div>
        <div class="start-dest">
          <span class="start-dest-label" data-i18n="start.d2_label">Documentation</span>
          <p data-i18n="start.d2_desc">The canonical source for installation, quickstart, guides, and CLI reference, in English and Indonesian.</p>
          <a href="https://krewire.com/docs" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="start-link">krewire.com/docs ↗</a>
        </div>
        <div class="start-dest">
          <span class="start-dest-label" data-i18n="start.d3_label">Source &amp; Releases</span>
          <p data-i18n="start.d3_desc">The core repository holds the Go packages and the kiw CLI. Versions are published as Git tags.</p>
          <a href="https://github.com/krewire/krewire/tags" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="start-link" data-i18n="start.d3_link">Release tags ↗</a>
        </div>
        <div class="start-dest">
          <span class="start-dest-label" data-i18n="start.d4_label">Contribution</span>
          <p data-i18n="start.d4_desc">Workflow, commit conventions, and quality gates are defined in the core repository's CONTRIBUTING.md.</p>
          <a href="https://github.com/krewire/krewire/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="start-link" data-i18n="start.d4_link">CONTRIBUTING.md ↗</a>
        </div>
        <div class="start-dest">
          <span class="start-dest-label" data-i18n="start.d5_label">Questions &amp; Bugs</span>
          <p data-i18n="start.d5_desc">Ask questions in GitHub Discussions. Report bugs in the issue tracker of the repository they affect.</p>
          <a href="https://github.com/krewire/krewire.com/discussions" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="start-link" data-i18n="start.d5_link">GitHub Discussions ↗</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHY CONTRIBUTE & CONTRIBUTOR PRIVILEGES -->
  <section class="benefits" id="privileges">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-head w-full text-center flex flex-col items-center justify-center">
        <div class="sub-badge" data-i18n="privileges.badge">Contributor Privileges</div>
        <h2 data-i18n="privileges.title">Lifetime Access to Krewire's Paid Ecosystem</h2>
        <p data-i18n="privileges.subtitle">True builders deserve shared ownership. By joining and actively contributing to the Krewire open-source collective, you earn lifetime access to our upcoming commercial sub-products and premium ecosystem tools.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="benefit-grid">
        <div class="benefit-card">
          <div class="benefit-badge" data-i18n="privileges.p1_badge">Core Privilege</div>
          <h3 data-i18n="privileges.p1_title">Commercial Sub-Products Lifetime Access</h3>
          <p data-i18n="privileges.p1_desc">Receive free lifetime licenses for upcoming commercial Krewire products — including managed cloud orchestration tools, enterprise modules, and premium services.</p>
          <ul class="benefit-list">
            <li data-i18n="privileges.p1_i1">Free lifetime access to all paid Krewire commercial sub-products</li>
            <li data-i18n="privileges.p1_i2">Priority early-access releases and exclusive roadmap previews</li>
            <li data-i18n="privileges.p1_i3">Direct private collaboration channels with core maintainers</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="benefit-card highlight-card">
          <div class="benefit-badge" data-i18n="privileges.p2_badge">Strict Requirement</div>
          <h3 data-i18n="privileges.p2_title">Active Contributions Required</h3>
          <p data-i18n="privileges.p2_desc">This privilege is a two-way commitment. Your access remains active as long as you regularly contribute and help nurture the ecosystem's growth.</p>
          <ul class="benefit-list">
            <li data-i18n="privileges.p2_i1">Submit PRs for new features, bugfixes, or kernel optimizations</li>
            <li data-i18n="privileges.p2_i2">Review open PRs and stress-test high-concurrency scenarios</li>
            <li data-i18n="privileges.p2_i3">Author KWF architecture specifications or comprehensive docs</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="benefit-card">
          <div class="benefit-badge" data-i18n="privileges.p3_badge">Revocation Policy</div>
          <h3 data-i18n="privileges.p3_title">Revocable if Inactive or Dormant</h3>
          <p data-i18n="privileges.p3_desc">To protect community fairness and true meritocracy, commercial access licenses may be revoked if a contributor becomes inactive or dormant over an extended period.</p>
          <ul class="benefit-list">
            <li data-i18n="privileges.p3_i1">Contributor activity and commits are periodically audited</li>
            <li data-i18n="privileges.p3_i2">Prolonged inactivity or dormancy leads to license deactivation</li>
            <li data-i18n="privileges.p3_i3">Access privileges can be promptly reinstated upon resumed contribution</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="meritocracy-callout mt-8">
        <div class="meritocracy-inner">
          <div class="meritocracy-icon">⚖️</div>
          <div class="meritocracy-body">
            <strong data-i18n="privileges.policy_title">Krewire Meritocracy Policy:</strong>
            <p data-i18n="privileges.policy_text">We believe those who lay the foundation should share in its fruits. Commercial access is free for all active contributors, provided ongoing dedication to the collective is consistently maintained.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 4-TIER MERITOCRACY PRIVILEGE LADDER (Issue #3) -->
      <div class="meritocracy-ladder-section mt-12">
        <h3 class="text-center font-bold text-xl mb-6">The 4-Tier Meritocracy Ladder</h3>
        <div class="ladder-grid">
          <div class="ladder-card">
            <div class="ladder-badge tier-1">Tier 1</div>
            <h4>Contributor</h4>
            <span class="ladder-req">1st Merged Pull Request</span>
            <p>Listed on community Wall of Fame, Contributor badge on Discord, and lifetime access to starter developer tools.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="ladder-card">
            <div class="ladder-badge tier-2">Tier 2</div>
            <h4>Collaborator</h4>
            <span class="ladder-req">5+ Merged Pull Requests</span>
            <p>Issue triage and labeling permissions, invitation to bi-weekly maintainer sync calls, and roadmap voting rights.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="ladder-card">
            <div class="ladder-badge tier-3">Tier 3</div>
            <h4>Maintainer</h4>
            <span class="ladder-req">Subsystem Owner</span>
            <p>Full review &amp; merge authority for designated repository/package, RFC voting power, and sponsored conference travel.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="ladder-card highlight-ladder">
            <div class="ladder-badge tier-4">Tier 4</div>
            <h4>Steering Committee</h4>
            <span class="ladder-req">Ecosystem Governance</span>
            <p>Security signing keys, foundation budget oversight, strategic industry partnerships, and grant disbursements.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- INTERACTIVE ONBOARDING PATHWAYS SELECTOR (Issue #3) -->
      <div class="pathways-selector-card mt-10">
        <div class="pathways-selector-head">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-lg mb-2">Choose Your Contributor Pathway</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted">Select your background to see curated tasks, recommended starter repositories, and architecture resources.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pathway-tabs flex flex-wrap gap-2 mt-4 mb-4">
          <button class="pathway-tab active btn btn-sm btn-primary" onclick="selectPathway('newbie')">🌱 New to Go?</button>
          <button class="pathway-tab btn btn-sm btn-outline" onclick="selectPathway('backend')">⚙️ Backend Engineer</button>
          <button class="pathway-tab btn btn-sm btn-outline" onclick="selectPathway('frontend')">🎨 Frontend &amp; UI</button>
          <button class="pathway-tab btn btn-sm btn-outline" onclick="selectPathway('devops')">☁️ DevOps &amp; Infra</button>
        </div>
        <div class="pathway-content" id="pathwayDetails">
          <div class="pathway-info">
            <h4 id="pathwayTitle" class="font-bold text-base mb-2">New to Go? (Beginner Friendly)</h4>
            <p id="pathwayDesc" class="text-sm text-muted mb-4">Start by polishing documentation in <code>krewire.com</code>, writing unit tests for <code>krewire/pkg/model</code>, or fixing starter bugs labeled <code>good first issue</code>.</p>
            <div class="pathway-links flex gap-3">
              <a id="pathwayCta" href="https://github.com/krewire/krewire/issues?q=is%3Aissue+is%3Aopen+label%3A%22good+first+issue%22" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm">Find Good First Issues →</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

